theory.intro:
Enlarge a right-angled triangle and every side gets longer, but the angles do not change and neither do the trigonometric ratios. That is why one stored value of $\sin 30^{\circ}$ is correct for every right-angled triangle containing a $30^{\circ}$ angle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (O1) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P1) at (3,0);
\coordinate (Q1) at (3,2.25);
\draw (O1)--(P1) node[midway,below] {$a$};
\draw (P1)--(Q1) node[midway,right] {$b$};
\draw (Q1)--(O1) node[midway,above left] {$c$};
\coordinate (s1) at ($(P1)!0.3cm!(O1)$);
\coordinate (s2) at ($(P1)!0.3cm!(Q1)$);
\draw (s1)--($(s1)+(s2)-(P1)$)--(s2);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.5cm,angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle=P1--O1--Q1};
\coordinate (O2) at (4.6,0);
\coordinate (P2) at (9.1,0);
\coordinate (Q2) at (9.1,3.375);
\draw (O2)--(P2) node[midway,below] {$ka$};
\draw (P2)--(Q2) node[midway,right] {$kb$};
\draw (Q2)--(O2) node[midway,above left] {$kc$};
\coordinate (t1) at ($(P2)!0.3cm!(O2)$);
\coordinate (t2) at ($(P2)!0.3cm!(Q2)$);
\draw (t1)--($(t1)+(t2)-(P2)$)--(t2);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.5cm,angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle=P2--O2--Q2};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

